        "abstract": "Switching power supplies (SPS) are often used in most electronic equipment. Due to its operation principle, SPS generate spurious currents called conducted emissions (CE). This work focuses in the study of CE for a type SPS known as flyback. In particular differential CE generated by common mode CE. It is being analyzed the possibility of reducing CE by a simple modification of SPS circuit in order to allow a simplified filter design looking for reduction in size and weight as much as possible, considering this is particularly relevant for reducing costs in certain applications. The reduction on CE levels for the proposed configuration is verified by simulation and measurement.",
